Subject: [PATCH 5.10.y 0/2] can: isotp: backport of 2 patches that failed to
 apply to 5.10-stable

This resubmits "can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent
NETDEV_UNREGISTER" (commit 20bab8b88baac140ca3701116e1d486c7f51e311
upstream), which failed to apply to the 5.10-stable tree, together
with "can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock"
(commit cf070fe33bfbd1a4c21236078fadb35dd223a157 upstream) from the
same upstream series, which builds on it and would otherwise fail
for the same reason. This is the full set of 3 upstream isotp.c
patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 1 already queued by the normal stable
process for 5.10 ("can: isotp: use unconditional synchronize_rcu()
in isotp_release()").

Both patches needed the same kind of adaptation already used for the
bcm.c patches on this branch: upstream's context in a few spots
includes code from unrelated, not-backported feature/refactor
commits that are not Cc: stable and not present on 5.10:

- the dynamic max_pdu_size TX buffer resize (commits 2f2dd39 "can:
  isotp: set max PDU size to 64 kByte", 2022, and 973bb01 "can:
  isotp: add module parameter for maximum pdu size", 2023)
- the hrtimer_setup() API consolidation (unrelated, generic hrtimer
  API change)
- the sk_error_report() wrapper (generic socket core API, not
  present here; kept sk->sk_error_report(sk) as used everywhere else
  in this file)

The corresponding hunks are omitted or adapted to the older code
shape; the actual race fixes themselves are unaffected and fully
applied. See each patch's changelog for the exact adaptation.

This assumes the 1 already-queued isotp.c patch for 5.10-stable has
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

Oliver Hartkopp (2):
  can: isotp: fix use-after-free race with concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER
  can: isotp: serialize TX state transitions under so->rx_lock

